# Pending-triage CVEs for the database image scan gate.
#
# Entries here are CVEs recorded as `under_investigation` in the OpenVEX
# document (docker/db/vex/simis-cms-db.openvex.json). Trivy's VEX filtering
# only suppresses `not_affected`/`fixed` statements, so pending entries live
# here, each with an expiry (`CVE-XXXX-NNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD`), until triage
# resolves them. When a CVE is triaged: update its VEX statement and remove
# its line here. A lapsed expiry re-fails the publish gate on the next run --
# deliberately, so triage cannot be forgotten silently.
#
# CVE-2026-16742 exp:2026-12-31
#   systemd-homed (not installed in this image). NOT pending triage: the VEX document carries a
#   not_affected statement for it (vulnerable_code_not_present, CVE_POLICY), added 2026-09-27.
#   This line exists because Trivy cannot apply that statement to one of the five packages.
#   Verified against the published image (simis-cms-db@sha256:39d6544d..., Trivy 0.73.0): the
#   statement suppresses libsystemd-shared, libsystemd0, systemd and systemd-timesyncd but never
#   libudev1 -- not when libudev1 is listed alone, and not even with a product-level statement
#   carrying no subcomponents at all, which suppresses the other four. Listing libsystemd0 alone
#   suppresses exactly libsystemd0, so the statement form is right; Trivy's VEX matching simply
#   never reaches libudev1 here (its dependency-graph path to the image root, most likely).
#
#   To resolve: after a Trivy upgrade, scan with the VEX and without this line
#   (trivy image --scanners vuln --severity CRITICAL,HIGH --vex docker/db/vex/simis-cms-db.openvex.json
#   <image>); if CVE-2026-16742 no longer appears, delete this entry. The expiry is a re-check
#   date for that, not a triage deadline.
CVE-2026-16742 exp:2026-12-31

# CVE-2026-76642, CVE-2026-78408, CVE-2026-78409, CVE-2026-78410 exp:2026-10-03
#   util-linux (no fixed version published by Debian bookworm). Entered 2026-09-03 to unblock
#   the publish gate, which had stopped delivery of two already-merged PRs (#1819, #1821).
#   Trivy reports 36 findings, all HIGH, no CRITICAL: these four CVEs against the nine binary
#   packages built from the one util-linux source (bsdutils, libblkid1, libfdisk1, libmount1,
#   libsmartcols1, libuuid1, mount, util-linux, util-linux-extra), so it is four defects
#   counted nine times each -- the same arithmetic recorded for CVE-2026-53613.
#
#   Pending triage, not a determination. What is already established, and why these are
#   expected to resolve not_affected on the existing recorded basis:
#
#   All four are privilege-boundary defects in mount/namespace operations -- a failed external
#   mount helper still running privileged X-mount post-hooks (76642), nsenter --join-cgroup
#   leaking root cgroup migration authority (78408), X-mount.subdir tree resolution escaping
#   via intermediate symlinks (78409), and restricted bind mounts not pinning their source
#   (78410). Each needs a caller able to cross a privilege boundary via mount or nsenter.
#
#   This image removes both routes, under mitigations already reviewed and recorded here:
#     - docker/db/Dockerfile runs `chmod u-s` on /usr/bin/mount, /usr/bin/umount, /bin/mount
#       and /bin/umount, so no setuid-root transition exists to race or subvert. This is the
#       mitigation recorded for CVE-2026-53613 (inline_mitigations_already_exist).
#     - The container drops all Linux capabilities (docker-compose.yaml cap_drop, CapEff
#       0000000000000000, PR #230), so it cannot perform mount or namespace operations at
#       all. This is the basis recorded for CVE-2026-53615.
#   nsenter is never invoked in the image, and PostgreSQL never mounts a filesystem.
#
#   That evidence is not a substitute for triage. tools/generate-db-vex.py keys its policy by
#   CVE precisely so a new util-linux CVE falls through to under_investigation rather than
#   inheriting a previous CVE's reasoning, and these four have not been assessed individually.
#   This entry holds the gate open for that assessment; it does not pre-empt its outcome.
#
#   Recorded in the VEX document as under_investigation on 2026-09-27 (PR #2056's merge), which
#   is the status these entries stand in for: Trivy does not suppress under_investigation, so
#   the entries still hold the gate open.
#
#   To resolve: assess each CVE against the mitigations above, add the outcome to CVE_POLICY
#   in tools/generate-db-vex.py, run `python3 tools/generate-db-vex.py` (no `>` -- the tool
#   writes the document itself, and a merge re-derives under_investigation statements from the
#   updated policy), confirm the statements read as intended, and delete these entries.
CVE-2026-76642 exp:2026-10-03
CVE-2026-78408 exp:2026-10-03
CVE-2026-78409 exp:2026-10-03
CVE-2026-78410 exp:2026-10-03

